# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/

# Python / host tooling — host artefacts, never image content. The web image ships no `scripts/` as
# files (the runner copies only `public/`, `.next/`, `node_modules/` and `package.json`): the JobSpy and
# LinkedIn workers run behind the VPS worker gateway.
#
# `scripts/` itself stays in the build context: the worker stage (`--target worker`) runs
# `npm run build:worker`, which needs `scripts/build-worker.mjs` and the shims beside it. The directory
# is a few hundred KB of sources — the bulk to keep out is the virtualenv and browser state that the
# host tooling creates in place, not the scripts themselves.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.venv/
**/.playwright/
**/browser-profile/
**/chrome-profile/

# Agent / project memory — not application content
.workbuddy-ai/

# Local browser caches — the app attaches to the VPS-hosted Chrome over CDP and ships no browser.
.playwright/
# TypeScript incremental build state from a local `tsc` run
*.tsbuildinfo

# Sensitive files
firebase-key.json
*.pem
*.key
*.csv
cookies.txt

